# Unpacked third-party archives
vendor/

# --- Brand authoring stays private ---------------------------------------
# design/ holds the brand portal, the mocks and the generator of the mark.
# None of that belongs in a public repository: a clone would otherwise carry the
# complete brand material — and trademarks are governed by different rules than
# the code that uses them.
#
# What the app needs in order to build is NOT in here; it is versioned inside
# the app tree: src/lib/brand/, src/brand.css, public/ (favicons, fonts) and
# src-tauri/icons/. A fresh clone therefore builds without design/ and without
# Python.
#
# NOTE: this leaves the generator on one machine only. design/ belongs in its
# own private repository or a backup — otherwise the mark is no longer
# reproducible after a machine change.
design/

# Local tooling configuration. .mcp.json wires up the TailGrids MCP server for
# this workspace — no credentials, but it is an editor setup rather than part of
# the project.
.mcp.json

# --- Agent guardrails -----------------------------------------------------
# .claude/hooks/state/ is runtime state: the unlock-window flags, the per-session
# edit trackers, the telemetry rings and the stored push verdict. All of it is
# local to one machine and one set of sessions; committing it would hand another
# clone stale flags and a verdict about a commit it never verified.
.claude/hooks/state/

# The user's own "stop reminding me" switch for a visual iteration loop.
.claude/iteration.lock

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. .claude/settings.json IS committed — it wires
# up the hooks and is part of the project.
.claude/settings.local.json
